{
 "_note": [
  "Local-language search terms for the currency listening sweep.",
  "",
  "WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. 89 of 133 currencies have an audience that does not",
  "read English. An English-only query undercounts them SILENTLY - a wrong or",
  "missing term returns zero, which reads exactly like 'nobody is talking",
  "about it'. So a zero here is never evidence of quiet; it is evidence of",
  "nothing until the term has been checked by someone who reads the language.",
  "",
  "TERMS ARE QUERY-READY PHRASES, not bare words. Several currency names are",
  "ordinary words in their own language and are worse than useless alone:",
  "  peso    = weight (Spanish)        sol  = sun (Spanish)",
  "  real    = royal/real (Portuguese)  leu  = lion (Romanian)",
  "  dong    = common word (Vietnamese) manat/som = shared across states",
  "Where that happens the term is qualified ('peso argentino') and",
  "`bare_unsafe` records why, so nobody 'simplifies' it later.",
  "",
  "CONFIDENCE is the author's, and it is honest rather than flattering:",
  "  high   - common term, common script, would bet on it",
  "  medium - correct to the best of my knowledge, worth a second pair of eyes",
  "  low    - plausible; DO NOT trust a zero result from these until checked",
  "Everything here was written from memory. Review before the sweep is read",
  "as evidence, and treat every low-confidence zero as unmeasured.",
  "",
  "Fields: terms[] query-ready phrases | confidence | bare_unsafe (optional)",
  "",
  "X NORMALISES, VERIFIED 2026-08-13 by searching both forms and comparing",
  "results. Accents fold (dolar finds dólar and vice versa) and plurals stem",
  "(pesos finds peso). So write ONE form - the accented singular - and do",
  "not add variants. Five redundant plurals were removed after this test.",
  "Irregular plurals that are not a simple -s (meticais, guaraníes) are kept",
  "because stemming was not verified for those, and a bare form that differs",
  "from a phrase already listed (colones against 'colón costarricense') is",
  "kept because a phrase never matches a bare word.",
  "",
  "SWEEP 1 CORRECTION (2026-08-14). The first sweep ranked Georgia above the",
  "Philippines and Sao Tome at 19,000 posts a week, because bare one-word",
  "terms here matched ordinary words: dobra is Portuguese for 'folds', soles",
  "is 'suns', bolivar is Simon Bolivar, piso is 'floor'. The terms were not",
  "deleted - listen_queries.py now routes every single-word term to the",
  "`loose` query, which is untrusted by construction, so the next sweep can",
  "measure how noisy each one is instead of guessing. Phrases still go to",
  "`tight`.",
  "",
  "Also removed: terms that merely mean 'dollar' in the local language. The",
  "dollar is what these are priced AGAINST, so such a term identifies no",
  "currency at all and matches every FX post in that language."
 ],
